 "notes": "WORDS: whole-word matches; matcher strips s/es/ed/ing/er/ers/y/ies, so base forms only, plus explicit forms where stripping would not reach the base (shitting, whored, raped, cumming, moronic, stupidest, dumbest, titty, titties). Contractions in phrases are written without the apostrophe (ill kill you, youre dead, im going to kill). Phrases that already contain a words or stems entry were removed as redundant. LEFT OUT ON PURPOSE (ordinary or too context-dependent): gay, queer, pansy, breast, nipple, penis, vagina, anus, rectum, semen, sperm, nude, naked, sex, sexy, hell, damn, bloody, fart, poop, balls, knob, bum, fanny, prick (finger-prick tests), hoe/hoes (garden tool), hooker (rugby), prostitute, pimp, slag (mining), gypsy, mzungu, haji/hajji (common honorific and name in Tanzania), infidel, savage, ignorant, fool, nonsense, rubbish, lame, crazy, cripple/crippled (economy), dik (dik-dik antelope), git (Git), tard (tardy), spic (spicy, because y is stripped), nig (Niger, because er is stripped), mick, gringo, redneck, groomer, shylock, monkey, baboon, ape, pig, dog, cockroach, witch, terrorist, nazi, hitler, anal (adjective), fecal, scat, snatch, skeet, cornhole, spastic is INCLUDED but spasticity is not. INCLUDED BUT CONTEXT-DEPENDENT (expect some harmless holds): ass (donkey, Bible), cock (rooster; 'cocky' also matches via y), dick (name), cum (cum laude), tit (tit for tat, birds), crap, piss, rape/raped/raping/rapist (news and legal discussion), pedophile/paedophile, negro (history), kafir/kaffir (religious term and cooking: kaffir lime), homo (homo sapiens), dyke (Offa's Dyke, sea walls), jap (japes), chink (chink in the armour), mong (monger), prat (prate), munt, chinaman (cricket term), coolie, sambo, hottentot, squaw, redskin, boner, clit, fap, perv, dox, loser, useless, pathetic, worthless, scum, dumb (also 'deaf and dumb'), stupid, idiot, moron, retard/retarded (also medical/historical use), midget, schizo, sissy, sodomite, shemale, horny, orgy, boobs, tits. NOT A STEM, WORDS ONLY (would hit ordinary words): nigger (snigger), niggar (niggardly), retard (retardant), cunt/cock/dick/tit (Scunthorpe-type hits), wanker (swanker), kaffir, beaner, mick, spic. 'nigger' therefore cannot be caught run-together by this list; the matcher needs a rule such as 'starts a token' for it. STEM RISKS: all 140 stems were checked against a 370,000-word dictionary (none sits inside an ordinary word) and for cross-word-boundary hits against the 10,000 most common English words. If the matcher removes ALL spaces before matching stems, the remaining possible false holds are: blowjob/handjob ('blow jobs', 'hand jobs'), jackoff ('blackjack offer'), dumbass ('dumb asset'), raghead ('drag head'), nutsack ('nuts acknowledge'), gangbang ('gang bang'), slopehead, analsex ('canal sexual'), upskirt ('cup skirt'), cameltoe, junglebunn, halfbreed ('behalf breeds'), christkiller, deepthroat (Watergate), xvideos. Stems starting with 'ass' (assclown: 'class clown', asswipe, asslick, assmunch...) and others such as nitwit ('unit with'), dimwit, halfwit, creampie ('cream pie'), horseshit ('horses hit'), dogshit, shemale ('she male'), wetback, dothead, dirtbag, ratbag were demoted to WORDS for that reason. Hindi/Urdu romanised abuse (madarchod, behenchod, bhenchod, chutiya, bsdk, gandu, haramzada, bakchod, maderchod) is included as a small extra because South Asian chat abuse appears in East African English comments; drop it if another list covers it. Caribbean (bloodclaat, bumbaclaat, rassclaat) and South African (makwerekwere, kwerekwere, kaffer, munt) terms are included for the same reason. Swahili and other Tanzanian-language terms are NOT in this file. SCAM list is hold-only and deliberately skips phrases that legitimate readers use on a Tanzanian education/finance blog: 'apply for a loan' (HESLB student-loan questions), 'registration fee', 'processing fee', 'recruitment agency', 'pass the exam', 'forex trading', 'pyramid scheme' (warnings), 'fake notes / counterfeit money' (awareness posts), 'wire transfer', 'million dollars', 'work abroad', 'witchcraft', 'contact the doctor'. Still likely to hold some honest comments: 'make money online', 'work from home job', 'crypto investment', 'bitcoin investment', 'visa sponsorship', 'essay help', 'homework help', 'assignment help', 'dear friend', 'click here', 'check out my', 'follow me on', 'hiring now', 'dating site', 'western union', 'cash app', 'limited offer'. PHRASES that are only abusive in some contexts but were kept because the brief asked for them: your mother / your mom / your mum / your mama and ur/yo variants, shut up, get lost, get a life, go to hell, 'death to', 'watch your back', 'dead meat', 'you suck', 'i hate you', 'you liar', 'you thief', 'you terrorist', 'you are a witch' (witch accusations can lead to violence in Tanzania). Phrase 'spic' alone is not possible (single word); dirty spic, filthy spic and you spic are the only spic entries."
